# vms-6b8e (SHOW SYSTEM matches oracle): the SHOW SYSTEM BANNER + COLUMN geometry
# on OpenVMS VAX V7.3. The process-list ROWS are inherently non-reproducible (the
# process set, PIDs, I/O, CPU, order all vary run-to-run -- even between fresh
# boots), so this surface pins only the STABLE layout: the banner structure
# (OpenVMS V#.# on node ... <date> Uptime <time>) and the fixed column-header row.
# NORMALIZE: digit-mask (masks the volatile date/uptime/version in the banner) AND
# drop the data rows (4,$d) -- leaving echo + banner + column header. The vms-c38
# gate applies the SAME mask to OVMX's SHOW SYSTEM before diffing (its process set
# also varies), so only a real banner/column-geometry divergence reds it. Per-row
# field geometry is separately documented in docs/oracle/vax73-show-system-process.md.
ARCH=vax
DESC="SHOW SYSTEM banner + column geometry (process rows dropped, volatile fields masked)"
NORMALIZE='s/[0-9]/#/g; 4,$d'
COMMANDS=(
  'SHOW SYSTEM'
)
